# Fixture for the `indexaliasguard` option (RE-friction need
# quadratic-transform-loses-four).  `transform` initialises the top four dwords
# of its own frame from a 128-bit constant in .rodata, then reads that buffer
# only through a pointer derived from LEA:
#
#     sub     $0x20, %esp
#     mov     coefficients+0, %eax
#     mov     %eax, 0x10(%esp)         # ... and three more, one per dword
#     ...
#     lea     0x20(%esp), %eax         # four pushes deep: the same 0x10 slot
#     xor     %ebx, -0x4(%eax)         # the loop walks it a dword at a time
#
# With `option indexaliasguard off` the four stores have no reader at all
# (every read reaches the slots through the LEA pointer), so ActionDeadCode
# deletes them and the emitted C declares `unsigned int v10 [4];`, XORs it
# through the pointer and never initialises it.  `load` (the default) restores
# upstream Heritage::guardLoads, which puts an addrforce COPY read of the range
# in front of the indexed LOAD, and the four assignments come back.
#
# The body is verbatim MSVC i386 output: 252 bytes at 0x401330 of decoder.exe
# from the sddecoder crackme (crackmes.one 5ab77f5f33c5d40ad448c820), with the
# 16 .rodata bytes it loads placed at their original 0x4060bc so the constants
# and the `&coefficients[i]` index expression are the ones the witness shows.
#
# Build:
#   as --32 -o /tmp/indexaliasguard_i386.o indexaliasguard_i386.s
#   ld -m elf_i386 -T indexaliasguard_i386.ld -o indexaliasguard_i386 \
#      /tmp/indexaliasguard_i386.o
#
